# Active Directory Sites and Services

## Objective

Configure Active Directory Sites and Services to represent physical network locations and optimize directory replication.

## Tasks Performed

- Created Active Directory sites
- Configured subnet objects
- Associated subnets with sites
- Created and configured site link
- Examined replication topology between sites

## Implementation

Sites were configured to simulate geographically distributed network locations.

Subnet objects were created and linked to their corresponding sites to allow domain controllers and clients to determine the closest authentication source.

Site links were configured to define replication paths between locations.

## Key Concepts

### Sites

Sites represent physical network locations within an Active Directory environment.

### Subnets

Subnets map client IP ranges to specific sites.

### Site Links

Site links define replication paths and schedules between sites.

## Benefits

- Reduced replication traffic
- Improved authentication efficiency
- Better representation of enterprise network topology

